## Add the official package

1. Open `{{CONTAINER}}` in Xcode.
2. Choose **File > Add Package Dependencies...**.
3. Enter `https://github.com/sparkle-project/Sparkle`.
4. Select the tested `{{SPARKLE_VERSION}}` release and add the `Sparkle` product to target `{{TARGET}}`.
5. Add `SparkleReleaseKit/AppUpdater.swift` to the same target when the project does not use file-system-synchronized groups.

SparkleReleaseKit deliberately does not rewrite arbitrary `project.pbxproj` files.

## Connect the lifecycle

For SwiftUI, keep the updater alive in the type marked `@main`:

```swift
@State private var appUpdater = AppUpdater.shared
```

For AppKit, keep it alive in the application delegate:

```swift
private let appUpdater = AppUpdater.shared
```

A manual **Check for Updates...** command may call:

```swift
AppUpdater.shared.checkForUpdates()
```

Preserve existing custom updater controllers, delegates, beta-channel logic, and user interfaces. Do not replace custom update code merely because a generated alternative exists.

