## Signature boundaries

- Sparkle EdDSA authenticates the exact update archive and is required in every release mode.
- Ad-hoc signing provides structural consistency for Free Mode but no verified developer identity.
- Developer ID and notarization are optional Apple trust layers.
- HTTPS protects transport and SHA-256 supports independent release review.

These mechanisms are complementary and are never reported as interchangeable.

